# NOTES
# 1. Steel-vessel Magnox stations misclassified as "(none)": Hinkley Point A, Hunterston A, and the Windscale AGR
#    prototype ALL had steel (or stainless steel) pressure vessels, contradicting the heuristic's blanket
#    "None" default for rpv_manufacturer. Oldbury and Wylfa correctly have "None" — they were the first two UK
#    stations to use prestressed concrete pressure vessels (PCPV), confirming the task brief's warning that early
#    Magnox stations differ from later ones on this exact field. Sizewell A and Trawsfynydd (also early Magnox)
#    could not be confirmed either way — flagged UNVERIFIABLE rather than assumed steel.
# 2. Turbine heuristic ("GEC" as blanket default) is wrong for the majority of Magnox stations: actual suppliers
#    were station-specific — English Electric (Hinkley A, Sizewell A, Wylfa), C.A. Parsons & Co (Hunterston A,
#    Hunterston B), AEI/C.A. Parsons jointly (Oldbury), Richardsons Westgarth (Trawsfynydd). GEC turbines were
#    confirmed only for the AGR stations checked (Hinkley B, Torness) plus the GEC-Alsthom JV at Sizewell B.
# 3. Consortium-naming complexity (as flagged in the task brief) is real and unresolved at the sourcing tier used
#    here: Wylfa's Wikipedia article names BNDC as main contractor in one place and TNPG as "reactor supplier" in
#    another — likely reflecting that TNPG was an umbrella grouping formed in 1962 that BNDC-style consortia fed
#    into, but the article doesn't reconcile this and neither source used here resolves it. Treat Wylfa/TNPG-vs-
#    BNDC as a known ambiguity, not a contradiction we adjudicated.
# 4. Hinkley Point C: heuristic constructor/architect_engineer of "EDF Energy" conflates the existing-fleet UK
#    operating company with "NNB Generation Company," the actual EDF/CGN joint-venture project entity building
#    HPC. Turbine heuristic "Alstom" is a legacy brand name — the current supplying entity is GE Steam Power
#    (Alstom's nuclear turbine business was acquired by GE in 2015); marked WRONG but this is a naming-lineage
#    correction, not a factual reversal. RPV heuristic "Mitsubishi Heavy Industries" is a clear miss — MHI is not
#    involved in EPR RPV fabrication; Framatome is confirmed as the vessel supplier via two independent sources.
# 5. Prototypes (Windscale AGR, Winfrith) have thin public sourcing beyond "designed by UKAEA" — turbine and RPV
#    fields mostly UNVERIFIABLE rather than guessed. Windscale AGR's constructor is UKAEA in the input but the
#    actual site works contractor was Mitchell Construction, a distinction the heuristic collapsed.
# 6. Trawsfynydd had a named building architect (Sir Basil Spence) separate from the nuclear architect-engineer
#    role (APC) — a reminder that "architect_engineer" in this dataset means nuclear engineering AE, not the
#    civil/aesthetic building architect, which existed as a distinct credited role at several UK stations.
